WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:02.711
♪♪

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:05.672
There have been rumors of an 
alliance at the edge of the galaxy.

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:07.716
There’s a tremendous amount of detail

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:10.135
that’s required
in bringing Foundation to life.

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:13.638
This season is a lot bigger 
than the first season in scale and scope.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.181
Everything’s so detailed.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.725
Everything’s put together so well. 

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:18.393
It's insane.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.647
The wardrobes, the set designs, 
they’re all completely brilliant.

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:26.109
We show this factory 
progression of technology.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:29.404
Roughly speaking, it takes us 
two years to make a season.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.573
Figure six months for pre-production,

00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:36.619
seven to eight months of filming and 
then close to a year of post-production.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.371
Because we have so many visual effects.

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:42.876
Our real goal on this show is to get
people that scope that they don't 
expect on television.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.878
♪♪

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:45.503
Hang on!

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.881
(Grunting)

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:55.972
♪♪

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.348
And, action!

00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:02.145
When I started Foundation, I decided that 
I want to film as much of it 
on-location as possible.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:07.233
I want the crew and the actors 
to feel the heat, to feel the wind.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:10.612
Because I felt that it would just 
make everything feel more real.

00:01:11.362 --> 00:01:12.322
Smart boy.

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:15.950
Season two is very much a story of 
asymmetrical warfare.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.621
The Foundation compared to Empire is a spec.

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:23.625
but, slowly but surely, the Foundation 
is gaining influence.

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:29.422
They’ve grown, and they’ve
taken over the outskirts of the galaxy.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.299
♪♪

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:34.677
The sets and the locations that we’ve been
on for both seasons have been

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:36.221
picked out so incredibly.

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:41.559
It helps us create the world and it makes 
it so much easier to be in the moment.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.479
Season two goes all over the place.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.440
There are a lot of new worlds
and they’re all very different.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:51.402
We’re able to find all these new planets 
and give them a unique look.

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:53.530
♪♪

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.240
We’re gonna return to Trantor.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.284
In Ireland, we had the main palace sets, 
the original Mural of Souls, 

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:01.454
and we built a new clone tank set. 

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.373
We’re also back in a different Synnax.

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:05.291
A Synnax that’s completely 
covered in water.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:07.710
♪♪

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.339
The world of Ignis, we had the
jungle in the Czech Republic,

00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:14.759
but there are oceans in Ignis. 
So those scenes were shot in the Canaries.

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:20.098
I spent three days on sand dunes, and
it was miles away from everywhere else.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.602
But we have so much fun on set. 
I love every second of it.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.397
We’re in the Summer Palace.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.400
We wanted the elements in 
this set to make it feel like

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:33.403
we were in this encore lot-type 
of jungle palace.

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:36.948
Whoever’s in charge, please can 
we end this charade?

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.367
I thought you might be the one to notice.

00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:42.704
Terminus, where the Church of Seldon is,

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:45.832
was actually shot in the old Skoda factory
in the Czech Republic.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:50.461
Terminus city is in Fuerteventura, 
and it’s just so real.

00:02:50.753 --> 00:02:55.133
It’s in the middle of an empty space, 
and they’ve built a village.

00:02:55.216 --> 00:02:58.178
It’s not difficult to imagine 
you’re on a barren planet.

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:02.891
A lot of the locations that we’ve chosen, 
the population in North America have

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:04.434
not seen or don’t know about.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:07.812
So that lets us spend more time in 
those locations

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:11.608
as our backdrops for all of the 
storytelling, as if it’s an alien world.

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:14.027
And we’re always trying to push the 
look of the show.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:18.072
♪♪

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:20.783
Wow. Look at you.

00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.911
♪♪

00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:26.289
The fashion in season two,
it’s just fantastic.

00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:28.416
Our costume designer, Jane Petrie,

00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:32.462
she and her team had to come up with 
thousands upon thousands of costumes.

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:34.672
We’re flying through nine planets,

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.800
there’s no through-threads, so we have to
come up with a whole new concept for each

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:41.471
planet and a new backstory for where 
the costumes have come from.

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:44.641
One of the things that we really wanted 
to do with season two with our

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:47.477
costumes was just explode 
the color palette.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.271
We’ve got these wonderfully 
lush reds that are

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:52.732
embodied by The Church 
of the Galactic Spirit.

00:03:52.815 --> 00:03:57.070
You’ve got these kind of rainbow colors 
that are embodied by Cloud Dominion.

00:03:57.195 --> 00:04:01.032
Compared to season one, it’s been really 
good to get outside more.

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:02.700
It’s a little bit brighter.

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:05.495
We go to more planets, so 
there’s a lot more variety.

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:07.956
♪♪

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:09.207
Welcome to Trantor.

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:13.503
This season’s Day is completely 
different than last season’s.

00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:15.546
Day has turned in his blue armor.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.340
He’s gotten a little more flamboyant.

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:19.092
Lee's wearing chainmail this season.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.718
Seldon! 

00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:25.265
Allow me to present, 
the doyen of the Trade Leagues:

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:28.851
Sareth the First. Sole descendant 
of Dominion.

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:30.895
♪♪

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:31.980
Cloud Dominion.

00:04:32.021 --> 00:04:32.522
(Ship lands)

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:36.192
They come from a place where they produce 
the best pigments in the galaxy.

00:04:36.317 --> 00:04:39.279
All the imperial blues in pure form.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:39.904
♪♪

00:04:39.904 --> 00:04:43.157
We had two slices of agate and worked 
them into our print.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.034
And we had these big billowing robes.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.207
The look of Queen Sareth and Enjoiner Rue 
and all of the Cloud Dominion is different
to anything I’ve ever seen.

00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:54.585
Cloud Dominion is the exact opposite 
of what Trantor is,

00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:57.380
which is blues,  classics 
and everything is so strict.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:01.968
And then you have these women come 
into this universe and everything is 
billowy and feminine.

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:04.137
♪♪

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.805
What brings you to our world?

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:10.893
For season two, the location that really 
has embedded itself in costumes 
would be Ignis.

00:05:11.561 --> 00:05:13.646
There’s an awful lot of the environment 
around them that

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.107
I felt would really be part 
of their clothing.

00:05:16.607 --> 00:05:19.986
And then we worked with all of the colors 
of the plant life and the vegetation.

00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:21.863
We need your help.

00:05:22.405 --> 00:05:25.658
I like my plan wherein we 
keep to ourselves.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:29.912
♪♪

00:05:29.912 --> 00:05:32.707
Foundation is the most complex show

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.002
in terms of post-production of any project
I’ve ever been involved with.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:41.007
On average, we have about four thousand 
visual effects shots per season.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.467
(Metallic sound as gun extends)

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.136
The goal is to get everything photo-real, 

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.307
to get spaceships to move like we think 
spaceships would really move,

00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:52.060
to get our creatures to have the same kind
of fidelity 

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.936
that any kind of animal
would in our world.

00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:55.396
(Growl)

00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:59.025
They have stories in me. Many stories. 
Would you like to hear one?

00:05:59.275 --> 00:06:02.695
Demerzel’s dungeon and how she’s been 
split into pieces

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:07.992
was based on the idea that she can heal 
herself and make herself 
whole at any point.

00:06:08.284 --> 00:06:13.247
So the prison had to reflect that she 
could be kept separated by glass panes.

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:16.250
And her circuitry was then sandwiched 
between them.

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:19.879
And then, on the outer slices, 
was her human form front and back.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:24.634
And painted her circuitry onto these glass
panes with LED lighting to make it feel

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:27.637
physical, and then my team will go back in
and we’ll augment

00:06:27.637 --> 00:06:31.057
and give it that little 
bit of extra love to make it feel real.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:36.729
We probably spend a couple of weeks 
coloring each episode.

00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:42.235
Going through shot by shot, trying to make
everything as artful as possible.

00:06:42.443 --> 00:06:43.903
It’s a highly technical process.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:47.865
You an change the mood of the scene by 
making it darker and blue.

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.660
Sometimes they’re shooting over three days
which,

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.703
one day it’s raining 
and the next day it’s not.

00:06:52.954 --> 00:06:56.416
So integrating all of those shots back 
together with visual effects shots

00:06:56.541 --> 00:06:58.376
requires a level of intricacy and detail.

00:06:58.376 --> 00:07:01.337
♪♪

00:07:01.337 --> 00:07:04.090
(Rock door opening)

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.299
And then you’ve got sound.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.178
We’ve got a sound team called Sound Dogs, 
who are incredible.

00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:14.100
Our job is to help supplement and 
exaggerate a lot of the visuals 
that we’re seeing.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:17.228
I think just a little at the head 
and then you’re good.

00:07:17.228 --> 00:07:22.108
This year there’s beaches, so now you’re 
dealing with waves and sounds that are 
clobbering the dialogue a bit

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.111
so you’re trying to clean all 
that up before Tyler’s part and his crew.

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:27.530
They’re creating sounds of ships 
that don’t really exist,

00:07:28.489 --> 00:07:29.073
creatures that don’t exist.

00:07:29.407 --> 00:07:30.450
(Creature moaning)

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.618
You’re building a sound 
world from scratch.

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:35.830
There’s always a sense of discovery 
in this process.

00:07:35.872 --> 00:07:39.208
I believe that post-production are 
one of the things

00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:43.504
that really makes Foundation feel 
different and more cinematic 
than your average show.

00:07:43.713 --> 00:07:44.630
♪♪

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.424
I think that’s kinda cool. Nice job guys.

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:49.135
Only Empire commands the stars. 

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.511
Crush them. Now.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:51.512
Shields forward!

00:07:51.512 --> 00:07:52.972
♪♪
(Gun's firing)

00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:56.309
I can’t wrap my head around the 
craftsmanship on this show.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:59.479
The attention to detail is 
just extraordinary.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.856
That you could only really get 
on a production like this.

00:08:02.023 --> 00:08:02.732
(Screaming)

00:08:03.608 --> 00:08:05.943
The stakes are much higher in season two.

00:08:06.861 --> 00:08:08.821
The galaxy has a countless 
number of planets.

00:08:08.863 --> 00:08:12.325
Ten thousand inhabited worlds, 
so we see more from this season.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.953
I didn’t think that it could 
get any more vast.

00:08:16.204 --> 00:08:20.666
And somehow, some way the team 
has made it even bigger.

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.377
In season two, the rocket takes off.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.588
And we’ve been having an absolute blast.

00:08:25.713 --> 00:08:27.215
♪♪

00:08:27.423 --> 00:08:31.469
It is such an incredible spectacle, 
and I’ve never seen anything like it.

00:08:32.136 --> 00:08:35.097
It’s time Empire had a reckoning.

00:08:35.389 --> 00:08:39.018
I am so grateful and lucky 
that I get to be a part of this.

00:08:39.101 --> 00:08:43.523
And I think we really succeeded 
in season two, and it was a real 
treat bringing it to life.

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:45.691
Get us out of here!

00:08:45.775 --> 00:08:47.944
♪♪

00:08:47.944 --> 00:08:48.736
Woo!

